[
    {
        "id": "basic_flow_tab",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "ESP32 MMDVM - Basic API Calls (All 11 Endpoints)",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "# ESP32 MMDVM Hotspot - Basic API Calls\n\nThis flow demonstrates simple HTTP requests to ALL 11 API endpoints.\n\n## Quick Start:\n\n1. **Update Base URL & Credentials:**\n   - Double-click any HTTP Request node (blue nodes)\n   - Change URL from `http://esp32-mmdvm.local` to your ESP32's IP\n   - Update credentials if different from defaults:\n     - Username: admin\n     - Password: pi-star\n\n2. **Test the endpoints:**\n   - Click any inject button to make a test call\n   - View JSON responses in the debug panel (right sidebar)\n\n## All 11 API Endpoints:\n\n### System Information\n- GET /api/status - Network & DMR status\n- GET /api/system-information - ESP32 hardware details\n- GET /api/modem-information - MMDVM modem firmware info\n- GET /api/system-status - System status overview\n\n### DMR Activity\n- GET /api/dmr-activity - Both slots activity\n- GET /api/dmr-slot1 - Slot 1 only\n- GET /api/dmr-slot2 - Slot 2 only\n- GET /api/dmr-history - Recent DMR transmissions\n- GET /api/rf-history - Local RF activity\n\n### Utilities\n- GET /api/logs - Serial monitor logs\n- GET /api/wifiscan - Available WiFi networks\n\n## Next Steps:\n\nOnce you've tested the basic calls, check out:\n- 02-monitoring-dashboard.json for a complete UI dashboard\n- 03-advanced-examples.json for alerts, logging, and integrations"
    },
    {
        "id": "comment_config",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "basic_flow_tab",
        "name": "CONFIGURATION - Double-click Function nodes to change URL (http://esp32-mmdvm.local) and credentials (admin/pi-star)",
        "info": "To configure:\n1. Double-click the function node\n2. Change URL to your ESP32 IP address\n3. Update username/password if different from defaults",
        "x": 400,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
